<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE gslv-f18-nvs03 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — GSLV-F18 / NVS-03 (SDSC-SHAR SLP) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Loft: GSLV-F15/NVS-02 PUBLISHED FLIGHT SEQUENCE (ANALOG, not this flight): time, altitude, Rel.Vel knots from ISRO&#x27;s F15 brochure
https://www.isro.gov.in/media_isro/pdf/GSLVF15/GSLV-F15_NVS-02_EngBrochure240125.pdf ; F18 uses the same GSLV Mk II, same ~2,250 kg NVS payload class, same 106 deg azimuth; ISRO has published no F18 event table.
Linear interpolation between knots; ground range = integral of sqrt(RelVel^2 - hdot^2) x R/(R+h) (the horizontal split is the only non-published assumption).
Knots: L40H shut-off 149 s/69.6 km, GS2 ign 149.6, GS1 sep 151.2, IS sep 157, PLF sep 237.42 s/115 km, GS2 shut-off 291.16 s/131 km, CUS ign 295.68, CUS shut-off 1135.38 s/302.46 km/9.707 km/s.
Azimuth basis: NAVAREA VIII 1127/26 (rocket launching 301700-302100Z Oct, launch point 13-43.20N 080-13.80E) zone centroids bear 106.09/106.31/106.75 deg from the pad;
used mean of zones 2-3 = 106.20 deg. ISRO F18 brochure &#x27;launch azimuth 106 deg&#x27; (https://www.isro.gov.in/media_isro/image/index/GSLVF18_NVS03/GSLV_F18_NVS03_Mission_Brouchure_27102026.pdf) agrees. NOTAM A3241/26 (VOMF) 30 Oct-11 Nov 1700-2100Z.
Target (F18 brochure): GTO 170 x 37,023 km, i 20.75 +/- 0.1 deg, AoP 178 +/- 0.5 deg; NVS-03 ~2,250 kg. F15 S/C separation was T+1150.38 s (not in file; F18 unpublished).
Velocity = d/dt of interpolated altitude and ground range (Earth-relative). Rhumb-line track is an approximation (real track curves toward the equator).
T0: LL2 NET 2026-10-30T18:21:00Z (Fri 30 Oct 11:21 am PDT), status Go; ISRO (X, 28 Oct): 30 Oct 2026 23:51 IST. Spaceflight Now&#x27;s schedule does not list it.
Pad (LL2): 13.719900N 80.230400E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=106.20 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-10-30T18:21:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
